# Commit after each feature

When a feature, bugfix, or user-requested change is finished and working:

- Create a git commit for that work without waiting to be asked.
- Follow the existing git safety protocol: never update git config, never force-push, never skip hooks, never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials).
- Stage only files that belong to the feature. Do not commit unrelated dirty files.
- Write a concise 1–2 sentence message focused on why the change exists.
- Do not push unless the user asks.

Do not commit incomplete or broken work, exploratory-only edits, or when the user explicitly says not to commit.
